  "question": {
    "text": "A particle gets displaced by $\\Delta \\bar{r}=(2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}+4 \\hat{k}) \\mathrm{m}$ under the action of a force $\\vec{F}=(7 \\hat{i}+4 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k})$. The change in its kinetic energy is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uGEnw",
      "text": "\n$38 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wjx5r",
      "text": "\n$70 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "g6UaF",
      "text": "\n$52.5 \\mathrm{~J}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZkoRi",
      "text": "\n$126 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to work-energy theorem, Change in kinetic energy $=$ work done $=\\vec{F} \\cdot \\Delta \\vec{r}=(7 \\hat{i}+4 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k}) \\cdot(2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}+4 \\hat{k})$ $=14+12+12=38 \\mathrm{~J}$",
    "image": null
  },
